Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:29:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Fix #5: sign out of the built-in browser only once
 nothing is using it

Settings -> Sign out deleted the WebView2 profile folder while the item
panel (and possibly a browser, download or Connect window) still held it
open, so the delete looped or left a half-removed profile.

- MainViewModel.SignOutOfBrowserAsync does it in order: refuse while a
  browser, download or Connect window is open (the main window reports
  which via BrowserProfileInUse); clear the accounts so background
  syncs stop asking for the browser; raise BrowserProfileReleasing so
  the main window shuts the item panel; close the hidden Helix and
  Procore pages with a 30 s pause (ProcoreSyncService.CloseBrowser now
  takes a pause like Helix); then delete the folder, retrying up to
  30 x 300 ms before reporting a problem.
- ItemPanel.Shutdown releases the WebView2 and leaves the panel ready
  to start a fresh page on the next item (started = false).
- MainWindow counts open BrowserWindow/DownloadWindow instances.
- README describes the new behaviour.

Manual check (no UI test harness): open a Helix item in the panel,
Settings -> Sign out -> completes within ~2 s, the panel closes, the
next refresh asks to sign in. With a browser window open, the button
says to close it first.

